-- title:
--   Level-q field maps into level-qℓ field, fixed by Γ(q)
-- statement:
--   Let $q, M', \ell \ge 1$ with $q$ and $M'$ coprime, let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero which is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of type $\{q\ell\}$, and let $\xi \in L$ be a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity. For a modulus $M$ and $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$, write `xHFunctionField` $M\,H$ for the subfield `qExpFunctionFieldC` $\mathbb{Q}$ of $\mathbb{Q}((Q))$ attached to the subgroup [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $M\,H$ of $SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ (the image in $\Gamma_0(M)$ of the preimage of $H$ under `gamma0Units` $M$), and `laurentBaseChange` $L$ for the $L$-subfield of $L((Q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of that field under $\mathbb{Q} \to L$; here `levelH` $q\,M'$ is the kernel of $(\mathbb{Z}/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/q)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq L((Q))$ equal to `laurentBaseChange` $L$ of `xHFunctionField` $((q\ell)^2M')$ (`levelH` $(q\ell)\,M'$). Then: (i) the ring homomorphism `qExpand` $L\,\ell$, which multiplies all Laurent exponents by $\ell$, carries every element of `laurentBaseChange` $L$ (`xHFunctionField` $(q^2M')$ (`levelH` $q\,M'$)) into $K$; and (ii) for every such $x$, every $w \in K$ whose underlying Laurent series is `qExpand` $L\,\ell\,x$, every $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb{Z})$ lying in both $\Gamma(q)$ and $\Gamma_0(M')$, and every $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ satisfying `IsLevelAutAt` $L\,(q\ell)\,\xi\,(q\ell)\,((q\ell)^2M')$ (`levelH` $(q\ell)\,M'$) $\gamma^{-1}\,K\,\tau$ — that is, for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ on [`CohCarrier.GammaH`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) $((q\ell)^2M')$ (`levelH` $(q\ell)\,M'$) of weight $k$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ (the series `intSeriesC` $\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$ nonzero), all $x' \in K$ with Laurent series the image of `intSeriesC` $\mathbb{Q}\,p_f\,/\,$`intSeriesC` $\mathbb{Q}\,p_g$, and all ring homomorphisms $\iota : L \to \mathbb{C}$ with $\iota(\xi) = e^{2\pi i/(q\ell)}$, the coefficientwise image $\iota(\tau x')$ times the $q$-expansion of $g \mid_k$ `conjElemN` $(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f \mid_k$ `conjElemN` $(q\ell)\,\gamma^{-1}$, where `conjElemN` $m\,\delta$ is the conjugate $\mathrm{diag}(m,1)^{-1}\delta\,\mathrm{diag}(m,1)$ — one has $\tau w = w$.
--
--   This is the elementary half of the identification of the image of the full level-$q$ modular function field under $Q \mapsto Q^\ell$ with the fixed field, inside the full level-$q\ell$ function field over $\Gamma_0(M')$ with coefficients in $\mathbb{Q}(\zeta_{q\ell})$, of the level automorphisms attached to $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; the converse inclusion, that fixed elements come from level $q$, is not asserted. It feeds the auxiliary level results used in the construction of the full-level Jacobian, among them [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_finite_subgroup_forall_mem_iff_exists_isLevelAutAt`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.AuxLevel.exists_finite_subgroup_forall_mem_iff_exists_isLevelAutAt).
